WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.839
In tutorial 8.3, you'll choose
the questions buyers ask AI,

00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:13.570
and keep that list tidy
as your market changes.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.420
First, scroll down AI visibility
to Your question panel.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.908
It lists every buyer question you
track, with its buyer role and market.

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:28.997
The tabs split them into tracked, not
asked, pinned, refused and switched off.

00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:32.807
A refused question shows why,
like naming another company,

00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:36.132
and Why questions are
refused explains the rules.

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:40.421
The filters show one topic,
buyer role, market or assistant.

00:00:41.415 --> 00:00:44.125
Here, Buyer role is set to CFO,

00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:47.050
so you only see the questions
a finance lead would ask.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.399
Next, add your own. Type
one question per line,

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:55.939
the way a buyer would ask an assistant,
then a buyer role, topic and market.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.933
Tick Pin them to have them asked
first, then click Add questions.

00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:04.854
Below, Track adds a real
question people already ask AI.

00:01:05.849 --> 00:01:11.189
To change a question, click its pencil. You
can edit the wording, buyer role, topic,

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:13.250
stage and market, then save.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.420
The pin keeps a question asked
first. Switch off stops asking it,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.863
but keeps it in your list.

00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:26.050
To change many at once, tick their
boxes. A bar shows how many are selected,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.038
with Switch off, Switch on,
Pin, Set topic and Delete.

00:01:31.037 --> 00:01:35.137
Set topic gives them all one topic,
which groups them in your filters,

00:01:35.187 --> 00:01:36.715
results and reports.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.965
Already have a list? Under
Import a question list,

00:01:41.015 --> 00:01:44.339
How should the file look opens
a short guide to the columns.

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:48.719
Then click Choose a file
and pick your spreadsheet.

00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:51.699
You see how many questions are
ready before you import them.

00:01:53.265 --> 00:01:57.140
Finally, the Not asked tab shows
questions over your panel size.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.711
They're kept, but they
aren't asked each week.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:05.014
To ask them too, click Change the
panel size, in your tracking settings.

00:02:06.769 --> 00:02:10.944
Now your panel tracks the questions
your buyers really ask, by topic,

00:02:10.994 --> 00:02:12.528
buyer role and market.

00:02:13.537 --> 00:02:17.782
So, review your questions, add your
own, edit, pin or switch them off,

00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:21.560
change many at once, import a
list, and check what isn't asked.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:28.322
Your questions are set. Next, set up
weekly AI monitoring in tutorial 8.4.
